{"name":"Milkweed","hex":"#e3e8d9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"milkweed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants that have a milky sap and have pods that split to release seeds with silky tufts.\nPrincipally of the genus Asclepias in order Gentianales, family Apocynaceae\nAlso of the genus Calotropis in order Gentianales, family Apocynaceae\nEuphorbia peplus and Euphorbia heterophylla, in order Malpighiales.","Principally of the genus Asclepias in order Gentianales, family Apocynaceae"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milkweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milkweed (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Milkweed is a 2003 young adult historical fiction novel by American author Jerry Spinelli. The book is about a boy in Warsaw, Poland in the years of World War II during the Holocaust. Over time he is taken in by a Jewish group of orphans and he must avoid the Nazis while living on the streets with other orphans. Despite being a historical fiction novel, Doctor Korczak, a minor character in the story is based on a real person named Janusz Korczak."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/MilkweedNovel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milkweed_(novel)","wikidata":"Q3859022"},{"title":"Asclepias","blocks":[{"text":"Asclepias is a genus of herbaceous, perennial, flowering plants known as milkweeds, named for their latex, a milky substance containing cardiac glycosides termed cardenolides, exuded where cells are damaged. Most species are toxic to humans and many other species, primarily due to the presence of cardenolides. However, as with many such plants, some species feed upon milkweed leaves or the nectar from their flowers. A noteworthy feeder on milkweeds is the monarch butterfly, which uses and requires certain milkweeds as host plants for its larvae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Danaus_plexippus_on_Asclepias_incarnata_4999.jpg/330px-Danaus_plexippus_on_Asclepias_incarnata_4999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepias","wikidata":"Q162153"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg/500px-Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg/1280px-Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg/500px-Monarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A monarch butterfly on swamp milkweed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonarch_Butterfly_Danaus_plexippus_Milkweed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg/500px-Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg/1280px-Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg/500px-Asclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Asclepias syriaca seed pods, upper image from August and lower from December","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAsclepias_syriaca_seed_pod.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Milkweed_sprout.jpg/500px-Milkweed_sprout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Milkweed_sprout.jpg/500px-Milkweed_sprout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Milkweed sprout, a few days after sowing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilkweed_sprout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Pepsis_sp_02.jpg/500px-Pepsis_sp_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Pepsis_sp_02.jpg/500px-Pepsis_sp_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male Pepsis grossa, a typical milkweed-pollinating wasp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APepsis_sp_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Bee_on_Antelope_Horn-April_2015.JPG/500px-Bee_on_Antelope_Horn-April_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Bee_on_Antelope_Horn-April_2015.JPG/500px-Bee_on_Antelope_Horn-April_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Honeybee on antelope horn (Asclepias asperula) showing pollinia attached to legs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABee_on_Antelope_Horn-April_2015.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Asclepias-albicans.jpg/330px-Asclepias-albicans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Asclepias-albicans.jpg/330px-Asclepias-albicans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAsclepias-albicans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b